An issue occurs when `opclasses` are used without explicit ordering because empty string suffixes cause extra trailing whitespace in column definitions (e.g. `"name" text_pattern_ops ` instead of `"name" text_pattern_ops`). We can fix this by checking if `col_suffixes` contains an actual suffix before appending it, or filtering out empty suffixes.

Here is the minimal code change to resolve the issue:

### File: django/db/backends/ddl_references.py
<<<<<<< SEARCH
